# ⚠️ RESTORED 2026-08-18. This file was replaced wholesale by PR #29
# ("ci-secrets-push-failure-fix") with generic boilerplate that arrived still
# wrapped in markdown code fences — lines 1 and 71 were literal ``` — i.e. pasted
# from an answer without being read. It dropped every pattern this repo actually
# needs and added Python/Java/Gradle ones it does not.
#
# What that removal exposed, measured with `git check-ignore -v` before restoring:
#   * .dev.vars            — wrangler's secret file. Its own header line says
#                            "(gitignored)", which had silently become false.
#   * backups/             — 33 D1 dumps, 3.1 MB, whose `users` table carries
#                            `hash` and `salt` columns. One `git add -A` would
#                            have committed every password hash in the project.
#   * raw/*                — the 382,107,380-byte CLO exports.
#   * !.env.example        — the negation, so the one env file that IS meant to
#                            be committed became ignored.
#
# The gitleaks gate would not reliably have caught it: on push it runs with
# `--log-opts=-1` and scanned 60 bytes on the run that shipped this.
#
# Its additions were not merely useless — `*.gz`, `*.zip`, `*.tar.gz` and friends
# would silently ignore legitimate committed assets. Deliberately NOT carried over.
# The only two worth having, .vscode/ and .idea/, are added at the end.

# dependencies
node_modules/

# builds
dist/
build/
.next/
.open-next/
.wrangler/
*.tsbuildinfo

# env — never commit secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# wrangler's local override file — holds secrets and local-only vars, and does
# NOT match the .env.* patterns above.
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*

# generated assets (reproducible via the asset pipeline)
tools/asset-pipeline/output/
output/

# raw CLO exports for local work. The N001 export is exactly 382,107,380 bytes —
# stated in bytes because "364 MB" and "382 MB" both appear in this repo's history
# and are the SAME number (364.4 MiB vs 382.1 MB). Neither was wrong; the unit was
# never given. Do not "reconcile" them.
#
# ⚠️ These are NOT reliably re-downloadable. The ingest bucket expires every object
# after 14 days (`expire-raw-uploads`, all prefixes) and scripts/backup-r2.mjs
# mirrors the MEDIA bucket only, so a raw export lives in exactly one place: the
# local copy described by raw/CANONICAL.json. Keep a second copy on other hardware.
#
# If an object does still exist, note the key has SPACES — the hyphenated form is
# the local filename, not the key:
#   wrangler r2 object get "run-apparel-viewer-ingest/cycling all colours.glb" --file raw/cycling-all-colours.glb --remote
#
# Test fixtures derived from one belong in tools/asset-pipeline/src/__fixtures__/
# and must be small enough to read in a diff (the wordmark alpha is 13 KB).
#
# `raw/*`, NOT `raw/` — git cannot re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY is
# excluded, because it never descends into it to see the negation. With `raw/` the
# `!` line below is silently dead; verified with `git check-ignore -v`.
raw/*
# …except the manifest, which is ~1 KB of metadata and is the whole point: it is
# what makes a local-only canonical copy verifiable rather than merely asserted.
!raw/CANONICAL.json

# local backups (D1 exports contain password hashes — never commit)
backups/

# test artifacts
playwright-report/
test-results/
# Playwright MCP scratch output (console logs, page snapshots). Same class as
# test-results/ above: regenerated on every run, never read by a gate.
.playwright-mcp/
.lighthouseci/

# codebase-memory-mcp index artifact (machine-local, rebuildable — see docs/AI-TOOLING.md)
.codebase-memory/

# Machine-local agent settings. Holds CBM_ALLOWED_ROOT, which is an ABSOLUTE path
# and therefore cannot be shared — settings.json does not expand ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}
# (or any other variable) inside its `env` block, verified against the Claude Code
# settings reference on 2026-08-06. The checked-in .claude/settings.json carries
# everything that IS portable: the permission allowlist and the pipeline guard hook.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Written by .claude/hooks/log-instructions-loaded.mjs — a per-machine measurement of
# which memory files loaded and why. Diagnostic, not shared state.
.claude/instructions-loaded.log
# Written by .claude/hooks/note-compaction.mjs and deleted by its partner
# recall-nested-instructions.mjs — a one-shot marker saying a compaction just
# happened, so the next prompt can name the nested CLAUDE.md files that did NOT
# survive it. Per-session state, never shared.
.claude/.compact-pending


# misc
.DS_Store
*.log

# generated by apps/viewer/scripts/copy-decoders.mjs
apps/viewer/public/meshopt_decoder.js
apps/viewer/public/draco/
apps/viewer/public/basis/

# Coverage output — regenerated by `pnpm test:coverage`, read by
# scripts/check-coverage.mjs. Never committed: a stale committed report would
# satisfy the gate’s presence check while measuring nothing.
coverage/

# Generated by `node scripts/sbom.mjs` — a CI artifact, not a source file.
sbom.cdx.json

# Editor directories. The one genuinely useful pair from the PR #29 boilerplate
# described above; nothing else from it was kept.
.vscode/
.idea/
